}
We're reusing the same helper method from the Upload function, but, this time, we're
simply calling a built-in method, ExistsAsync, to determine whether or not the file is
there.
Finally, we have the RenameFile method:
public async Task<bool> RenameFile(string name, string oldName)
{
var blobNew = GetBlockBlobReference(name);
var blobOld = GetBlockBlobReference(oldName);
if (await blobNew.ExistsAsync()) return false;
await blobNew.StartCopyAsync(blobOld);
await blobOld.DeleteAsync();
return true;
}
Since there is no built-in method to rename a file, we just copy the contents and delete the
original. Obviously, should the new name already exist, the task would fail.
